<%- include('../partials/header', { title: 'The Chronicle' }) %>
<%
  const german = A.german;
  const flag = name => [...german].some(g => String(name).includes(g)) ? '🇩🇪' : '🇺🇸';
  const dollars = n => (n == null ? '' : '$' + Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US'));
  const champByYear = {};
  for (const c of A.champions) champByYear[c.year] = c;
  const years = [];
  for (let y = 2026; y >= (A.lore.foundingYear || 2016); y--) years.push(y);
  // Season pages exist where box scores do (2023-2025); the pre-Sleeper years
  // (2016-2022) share one ceremonial chapter at /history/early. 2026 is live,
  // no page yet.
  const linkFor = y => A.byYear[y] ? `/history/season/${y}` : (y >= 2016 && y <= 2022 ? '/history/early' : null);
%>

<div class="chron">
  <!-- 1. HEADER (turnover-corrected eyebrow) -->
  <p class="chron-eyebrow">Est. 2016 · Not Quite the Same Ten Men · A Decade of Receipts</p>
  <h1 class="chron-title">The <span class="gold">MFGA</span> Archive</h1>
  <p class="chron-sub">Every dollar, every champion, every humiliation — written down at last.</p>

  <!-- 2. THE STORY OF THE LEAGUE (the centerpiece) -->
  <div class="card">
    <div class="body">
      <div class="chapter">
        <p>It began, as the great institutions do, with a dick joke. In
        <strong>2016</strong> ten men put down a hundred dollars apiece and founded
        the <strong>Balls and Wieners League</strong> — a name chosen by grown adults
        with jobs. <strong>David</strong>, the German who has bitched about every
        buy-in increase since, won the very first one, which is the funniest possible
        result: the man who hates paying got paid first. What follows is the whole
        decade, year by year, every dollar and every humiliation. Each season links
        to its full chapter. Start at the top; it only gets worse for everyone.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2017–2018 — the Cory interregnum.</a></strong>
        The commissioner-to-be won back-to-back, the only dominance he will ever
        taste, which is presumably why he later built a website that goes strangely
        quiet after 2018. The buy-in ticked to <span class="stat">$125</span> then
        <span class="stat">$150</span>; the German objected both times, on schedule.
        Somewhere in these dim years the league renamed itself the <strong>Whiny
        Little Bitch League</strong>, and — in the dark, unrecorded — swapped three
        owners: <strong>Sam</strong>, <strong>Dylan</strong> and <strong>Jeremy</strong>
        took the chairs of <strong>Brandon</strong>, <strong>Taylor Hagen</strong>
        and <strong>Ben</strong>, who the ledger has all but erased.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2019–2021 — the reign of Marian.</a></strong>
        Then one man simply took the thing and would not give it back. A clean,
        undisputed <strong>three-peat</strong> — 2019, 2020, 2021 — worth $600, then
        $750, then $900 as the pot swelled beneath him. For three straight years
        every other owner was playing for second. It is the most dominant run in
        league history, and the only one nobody argues about.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2022 — the asterisk.</a></strong> Marian's
        fourth banner, and the one the league will fight over until it dies. In the
        final week the Bills–Bengals game was cancelled after Damar Hamlin's on-field
        cardiac arrest; Marian was losing, the game vanished, and he and
        <strong>Sam</strong> agreed to split the top two prizes. Stated once, plainly,
        with respect: that is what happened. The joke, forever, is the disputed ring
        and the decade of arguing — never the reason. It carries the asterisk on
        every board on this site.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/season/2023">2023 — the dynasty begins, the
        commissioner steals one.</a></strong> The Whiny Little Bitch League's last
        year, and the year it quietly added the <strong>weekly-high $100</strong>
        that is now the biggest money in the pot. <strong>Michael</strong> won it
        clean — a league-best 95–40 all-play — the first brick of a real dynasty.
        And <strong>Cory</strong>, running <em>Herbert the Pervert</em>, laundered
        the <em>worst-scoring roster in the money</em> (a .422 all-play) into 9–6 and
        a playoff check. A heist, certified by the man who ran the heist.
        <a href="/history/season/2023">The full 2023 chapter →</a></p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/season/2024">2024 — the rebrand, and Cory by
        8.20.</a></strong> The league became <strong>Make Football Great Again</strong>
        and finally added <strong>keepers</strong>. <strong>Jeremy</strong> the
        doctor diagnosed the field and took the ring; <strong>David</strong> won the
        regular season on the flimsiest luck in the league and choked to fourth in
        the playoffs; and the commissioner, in <em>Zero Mistakes Were Made</em>,
        missed the playoffs by <span class="stat">8.20</span> points while leaving
        <span class="stat">297</span> on his own bench. He built the scoreboard and
        benched his own money on it. <a href="/history/season/2024">The full 2024
        chapter →</a></p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/season/2025">2025 — the dynasty confirmed, and
        Richard crucified.</a></strong> <strong>Michael</strong> went 12–3 for a
        second ring in three years and the richest single season on record
        ($1,325). But 2025 belongs to <strong>Richard</strong>, who scored
        <span class="stat">1,711</span> points — third-most in the league — and
        finished <em>dead last</em> at <span class="stat">4–11</span>, the largest
        robbery the archive has ever measured. Cory, meanwhile, named his team
        <em>Scheisse</em> and went 5–10, which is German for "accurate."
        <a href="/history/season/2025">The full 2025 chapter →</a></p>

        <p><strong>2026 — in progress.</strong> The buy-in is $400 with a vote on
        the floor to make it five (the German is, we assume, apoplectic). And a
        decade in, this thing finally has a website that remembers <em>every single
        dollar</em> anyone has ever won or lost. The full constitution — the buy-in
        ladder, the payout revisions, the roster changes and the pending votes —
        lives in <a href="/history/amendments">the Amendments</a>. Everything else is
        the seasons below. Read them and weep, or read them and gloat. Those are the
        only two options this league has ever offered.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 3. THE SEASONS timeline -->
  <div class="card">
    <h2>📖 The Seasons <span class="sub">tap a year with a chapter</span></h2>
    <div class="body">
      <div class="timeline">
        <% for (const y of years) {
             const c = champByYear[y];
             const href = linkFor(y);
             const written = chapters.has(y);
             const preSleeper = y < 2023;
             const inProgress = y === 2026;
        %>
          <% if (href) { %><a class="tl-row" href="<%= href %>"><% } else { %><div class="tl-row tl-dead"><% } %>
            <span class="tl-year"><%= y %></span>
            <span class="tl-mid">
              <% if (inProgress) { %>
                <span class="tl-champ tl-live">Season in progress</span>
              <% } else if (c) { %>
                <span class="tl-champ">🏆 <%= c.champion %> <span class="flag"><%= flag(c.champion) %></span><% if (c.asterisk) { %><a class="aster" href="#asterisk" onclick="event.stopPropagation()">*</a><% } %></span>
                <% if (c.payout != null) { %><span class="tl-won"><%= dollars(c.payout) %></span><% } %>
              <% } %>
            </span>
            <span class="tl-tag">
              <% if (written) { %><span class="tag">Chapter</span>
              <% } else if (A.byYear[y]) { %><span class="tag pending">Records</span>
              <% } else if (preSleeper) { %><span class="tag ghost">Pre-Sleeper</span>
              <% } %>
            </span>
          <% if (href) { %></a><% } else { %></div><% } %>
        <% } %>
      </div>
      <p class="tl-note">Full box scores survive from <b>2023</b> on. 2016–2022 are the age before Sleeper — champions and money only; their chapters are on the way.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. FOUR DOORS -->
  <div class="doors">
    <a class="door" href="/history/records">
      <span class="door-icon">📖</span>
      <span class="door-title">The Record Book</span>
      <span class="door-sub">All-time highs, lows, the dynasty tracker, and every franchise page.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="door" href="/history/money">
      <span class="door-icon">💰</span>
      <span class="door-title">The Money Board</span>
      <span class="door-sub">Career earnings, ranked ten deep. The table that settles arguments.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="door" href="/history/badbeats">
      <span class="door-icon">💔</span>
      <span class="door-title">Bad Beats Hall of Fame</span>
      <span class="door-sub">Auto-detected heartbreak — the tragedies the schedule authored.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="door" href="/history/catalogue">
      <span class="door-icon">🃏</span>
      <span class="door-title">The Absurdity Catalogue</span>
      <span class="door-sub">Every box score mined: kickers over QBs, benched studs, near-misses.</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. THE 2022 ASTERISK (closing footnote) -->
  <%- include('_asterisk') %>

  <p class="provenance">
    Derived from the master sheet (<%= A.provenance.master_sha256.slice(0, 12) %>…)
    and the Sleeper harvest of <%= (A.provenance.harvest_built_at || '').slice(0, 10) %>.
  </p>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
